  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-uncertainty design choice is whether multiprofile + transformer aggregation meaningfully improves over singleprofile in a multimodal setting. config_004 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) directly tests this question while using moderate-cost encoders (resnet50, scvi_n200) to keep GPU hours in the middle range of the search space. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can exploit by upgrading to imagenet_vit_l or scgpt; if it underperforms, I learn that the aggregation complexity is not paying off and can pivot to singleprofile or avgpool variants. This gives the most information per unit cost in experiment 1, establishing a strong reference point for the remaining 9 experiments. Expected relative cost: moderate—higher than singleprofile configs due to transformer aggregation over multiple profiles, but lower than configs using imagenet_vit_l or scgpt."
}

